WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:16.010
Superhero casting news is everywhere, and it
changes at the drop of a hat. One day you

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:19.050
hear that they're adapting your favorite
comic book and the next day you hear

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.450
that Mr. Mom is cast as Batman or Gilbert
Grape is gonna be Spider-Man. Who could

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.780
have ever imagined that a 6'2" Australian
musical theatre actor was going to be

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:32.480
Weapon X. It's hard to picture him not
being Wolverine. Well, he almost wasn't.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.100
DOUGRAY SCOTT AS WOLVERINE

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.040
It's pretty difficult to imagine anyone but Hugh

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:43.330
Jackman as Wolverine, but before filming
started on 2000's X-Men, Dougray Scott was

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:47.120
set to wear the claws. But scheduling
conflicts with Mission Impossible 2

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.710
meant director Bryan Singer went to the
next name on the list:

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:54.410
Jackman. Wolverine fans the world over
remain grateful.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.180
JOHN KRASINSKI AS CAPTAIN AMERICA

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.780
Chris Evans has a
monopoly on comic characters, having been

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:05.519
cast as the Human Torch, Jake Jensen in
the adaptation of The Losers, and of

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.840
course, Captain America. But before Evans
got the job, the favorite was

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.320
John "Jim from The Office," Krasinski.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.100
I haven't read my Marvel handbook in a while, but I'm pretty

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:18.590
sure sarcastically mugging for the
camera isn't one of Captain America's

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:19.490
super powers.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.040
JAKE GYLLENHAAL AS SPIDER-MAN AND BATMAN

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.180
Tobey Maguire owned the role of Spider-Man in 2002's
film of the same name. But when his

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:31.799
health put him in danger of missing the sequel, director Sam Raimi cast

00:01:31.799 --> 00:01:35.659
Jake Gyllenhaal. When Maguire was deemed
healthy enough to spin webs, Gyllenhaal

00:01:35.659 --> 00:01:40.390
was sidelined. The actor also recently
revealed he tried, and failed, to secure

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:43.810
the Batman role that eventually went to
Christian Bale.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.180
TOM CRUISE AS IRON MAN

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.460
Robert Downey Jr. might well be one of
the few actors who was born to play a

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:54.381
particular superhero. There was no doubt
that he was the right man for the Iron

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:59.210
Man job. Amazingly, Tom Cruise was first
in talks to wear the armor. He was in

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:03.140
talks with Marvel for years, but when the
time finally came to make the movie, he

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.380
lost interest.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.260
MARLON WAYANS AS ROBIN

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:11.720
Director Tim Burton was slated to make a
third film in his Batman franchise. Comic

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.450
actor Marlon Wayans was cast as Robin,
and was set to get going after being

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:19.380
costume tested. But when Warner Bros. replaced Burton with Joel Schumacher,

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.990
the production started from zero. Wayan's contract was paid despite the fact that

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:26.770
the new movie cast Chris O'Donnell as
Robin.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.200
NIC CAGE AS SUPERMAN

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.400
After he parted ways with Batman

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:35.250
Burton was planning on making Superman Lives starring Nicolas Cage with a

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:40.280
script by Clerks director Kevin Smith. Thankfully, it never got off the ground

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:44.120
As bad as the last few Superman movies have been, they're head and shoulders above

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.340
what this could have been.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.840
BROOKE SHIELDS AS SUPERGIRL

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:54.060
On the subject of Superman, remember the bizarre Supergirl movie from 1984, with space wizards and

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.700
stuff? Before Helen Slater, Brooke Shields
was in talks to don the cape. The

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.900
director wanted to go with an unknown, so Shields was out.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.420
ADRIANNE PALICKI AS WONDER WOMAN

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.240
This one technically counts. Even
though Adrianne Palicki actually filmed

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:13.100
the pilot, the David E. Kelley produced series was canned before it could even air. It's

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.040
too bad, since it could have been a
winner.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.260
COMMON AS GREEN LANTERN

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.600
For a few years, Mad Max director George Miller was working on creating a Justice League

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:27.350
film, back when The Avengers was just a gleam in Disney's eye. Rapper/actor Common was

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:31.480
set to take on the role of Green Lantern
John Stewart, but the project was scrapped

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.300
and Common never got a ring.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.720
BRADLEY COOPER AS GREEN LANTERN

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:40.520
On the subject of Green Lantern, Warner Bros. eventually went with a solo movie for

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:46.320
this character. Before Ryan Reynolds won the part, Bradley Cooper auditioned, and tanked it.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:51.060
WB's loss, considering that Cooper
earned an Oscar nomination in 2012 and

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.710
Green Lantern tanked hard.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.960
EMILY BLUNT AS BLACK WIDOW

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.620
If you have any doubts that Emily Blunt could have pulled off Black
Widow, we urge you to check out her

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:04.239
badass role as Rita in Live Die Repeat.
Blunt originally had the part of Black

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:08.330
Widow in Iron Man 2, but had to bow out
due to contractual obligations, and the

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.700
role was handed over to Scarlett
Johansson.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.780
The movie she was obligated to do instead?

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:15.820
Gulliver's Travels. We feel for you Emily.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.220
JIM CAVIEZEL AS CYCLOPS

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:22.880
Bryan Singer originally offered Caviezel the role of Cyclops, but Caviezel turned it down to

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.210
star in the movie Frequency instead. Sure, he missed out on being a cast mainstay in

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:32.030
some of the better X-Men movies, but he
also avoided being in Last Stand. So we'd say

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:36.060
that's a bullet dodged there. Also, Caviezel went on to act as everyone's favorite

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.660
superhero, Jesus!

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:40.320
LEONARDO DICAPRIO AS SPIDER-MAN

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:46.960
In the '90s, Sony got the rights to Spider-Man and wanted Leonardo
DiCaprio, fresh off the Titanic, to play

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:51.000
your friendly neighborhood wall crawler. He ultimately turned the role down,

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.260
and the project was reworked with Tobey Maguire as Spidey.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.060
WILL SMITH AS SUPERMAN

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:02.680
Back in the long, long ago, Kevin Smith was set to direct a Superman movie. Producer Jon

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:06.780
Peters wanted Will Smith to portray
Clark Kent, but the movie never panned out.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.560
When Bryan Singer started work on
Superman Returns, he offered the role to

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:14.800
Will Smith again. Smith turned down the
offer, saying "You mess up white people's

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.700
heroes in hollywood, you'll never work in
this town again."

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.940
BILL MURRAY AND EDDIE MURPHY AS BATMAN AND ROBIN

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:27.880
In 1983, before Tim Burton was signed on to direct Batman, Ivan Reitman was attached to direct. He wanted

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:33.419
to cast Bill Murray as Batman and
Eddie Murphy as Robin. In 1986, Tim Burton

00:05:33.419 --> 00:05:37.259
was brought on to direct and had the
script rewritten, writing Robin out.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.520
Thanks for watching!

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.620
Don't forget to like and subscribe if
you want more.

